description:
**What:** Wire send_message() into the run() event loop: check flag, call send, handle success/error, clear stale errors on tick.

**Algorithm:**
1. In run(), after the tokio::select! block and before the chat-selection-change check, add:
   if state.should_send_message {
     state.should_send_message = false;
     let body = state.input.trim().to_string();
     if !body.is_empty() {
       if let Some(chat_id) = state.chat_ids.get(state.selected_chat).cloned() {
         match send_message(&http_client, &api_url, &chat_id, &body).await {
           Ok(_msg_id) => {
             state.input.clear();
             state.input_cursor = 0;
             // Message will appear via SSE state change
           }
           Err(e) => {
             let msg = sanitize_display(&format!('Send failed: {e}'));
             state.set_error(&msg);
           }
         }
       }
     }
   }
2. In the tick arm of tokio::select!, call state.clear_stale_error() on every tick.
3. When there are no chat_ids (empty list), Enter/send does nothing — already gated by the if let Some(chat_id) check above.

**Defensive rules:**
- Reset should_send_message BEFORE calling send_message (prevents double-send if user hammers Enter).
- sanitize_display() applied to ALL error strings before they reach set_error.
- Do not append the sent message locally — it will arrive via SSE Message state change.
- trim() the body before sending (guards against whitespace-only slip-through).
- input.clear() must ONLY be called on Ok, NEVER on Err.
- Do not block the event loop on send; awaiting is fine because run() is async.

**Agent team:** R reads current run() loop structure; I wires in the changes; T writes integration tests with wiremock for run()-level behavior; V runs full cargo test -p kith-tui.
